<title>POLAND: Polish macroeconomic forecast for Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>Polish macroeconomic forecast for Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a macreconomic forecast for the first quarter of 1997, submitted January 21, prepared for Reuters by Tadeusz Chroscicki, chief analyst at the Government's Centre for Strategic Studies (CSS):</p>
<p>MAIN ECONOMIC INDICATOR FORECAST</p>
<p>				DECEMBER    JANUARY    FEBRUARY MARCH</p>
<p>CPI (pct change)   month/month		 1.3(R)	2.7	  1.8	  1.4</p>
<p>  year/year		  18.5(R)     17.8	 18.1	 18.0</p>
<p>  Previous Dec = 100    118.5(R)    102.7	104.6	106.1</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT   month/month		 2.1(R)     -5.0	 -3.0	 10.0</p>
<p>  year/year		  10.1(R)     10.0	  9.0	 11.0</p>
<p> UNEMPLOYMENT RATE (pct) 13.5-13.6   13.7	 13.8	 13.9</p>
<p>Following figures in billion USD  OFFICIAL RESERVES	 18.0	 18.0	  17.9	 17.6</p>
<p> NET RESERVES		21.8	 21.8	  21.7	 21.5</p>
<p> C/A TRADE BALANCE*	-8.1	 -1.0	  -1.5	 -3.0</p>
<p>  Exports*		   24.1	  1.9	   4.0	  6.0</p>
<p>  Imports*		   32.2	  2.9	   5.5	  9.0</p>
<p>		    *********************************</p>
<p>NOTES: Official forex reserves are hard currencies held by the central bank while net reserves are the total amount of foreign exchange in the banking system. Indicators marked (R) are results, rest are forecasts. * Counted from start of year. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780</p>
